  "summary_en": "Bangladesh's 2020 national AI strategy (\"AI for Innovative Bangladesh\") sets seven priority sectors and six strategic pillars: R&D, workforce skilling, data infrastructure, ethics/privacy/regulation, start-up funding and industrialization. It includes a 2020–2025 roadmap. Robotics and autonomous vehicles appear only in passing; regulation is mainly deferred to future laws.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Six strategic pillars with a 2020–2025 roadmap and lead ministries",
   "Seven priority sectors: public services, manufacturing, agriculture, mobility, education, finance, health",
   "Plans to establish a National AI Research Center, AI sandbox and National AI Task Force",
   "Plans for data ethics and privacy laws and a Right to Explanation guideline for AI algorithms",
   "Goals to train 50,000 workers and fund 1,000 AI start-ups within five years"
